WEBVTT

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:04.330
Sharla, you can't give up!

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:45.880
What is this?

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.610
Everyone, wake up. Wake up!

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.240
What's wrong, Luna?

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.930
Is it already morning?

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.190
Shut up already.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.840
Listen. There's a noise from outside.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.710
But I don't hear anything.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.660
Maybe you're hearing things.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.330
Nothing like that. I definitely heard it!

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.430
Right, Kaoru?

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.270
But I definitely can't hear anything.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.880
That's strange...

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.910
What's wrong, Sharla?

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.140
Sharla!

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.610
The window! There's something there!

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.680
Don't surprise us like that. There's nothing there.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:56.980
What was that?

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.340
There <i>is</i> something there after all!

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:01.860
Don't tell me it's yesterday's...

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:02.870
What did you say?

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.680
No! No! No!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.020
Shut it! I'm telling you to shut up!

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.620
It seems to have stopped.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.270
How is it?

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.810
I can't see anything through the fog.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.470
We'll be eaten! We're all going to be eaten!

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:43.840
Calm down, Sharla.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.650
We can't be sure it's the thing from yesterday.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:47.700
But...

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:51.280
Yak yak yak yak, noisy chick.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.090
What's it doing?

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.850
Is it trying to break the shuttle?

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.410
We're not very delicious in here.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.100
Papa!

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:47.760
It seems to have left.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:50.340
We're saved.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:15.110
In any event, it's big.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.730
I've never seen a footprint this big.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.710
For this hard shuttle to be dented like this...

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:27.190
The fact that there's a footprint means that it's a
different creature than the snake we saw yesterday.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:32.080
Yeesh! If it's not one, it's another.
What's wrong with this planet?

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:35.380
Based on the size of the footprint,
its height is thirty meters.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:37.930
Thirty metres?

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.960
No, maybe fifty metres.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.230
Fifty metres?

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.310
Ten metres, tops.

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:51.680
Damn you!

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.180
What do we do now?

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:54.490
Let's see...

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.680
Isn't it obvious? We hurry up and fix the shuttle!

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.380
And get off this planet!

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.750
That's impossible.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.040
Why?

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:06.080
The shuttle's propulsion system's totally busted.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:11.290
Even if we fixed it, the shuttle's power alone
isn't enough to get us out of the gravity well.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.020
Seriously?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.760
If you got it flyin', I'd be worried.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.960
What?

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.450
The problem is where we are.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:20.640
Does it seem like the communication system can be fixed?

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.370
I can't say anything about it.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.990
Even if it's fixable, it'd take time.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:27.830
Just give it your best shot.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:31.280
He's supposed to?

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:36.470
Everyone, please listen.

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:41.830
If there's any civilized creatures on this planet,
then we may be able to get out of here.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.280
But it seems like we'll probably be here for a while.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.140
Everyone, please bear that in mind.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.450
Now that that's settled, we'd better
hurry up and find food and water.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.730
Before that, everyone get your belongings
and pool them together again.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.690
Let's check what kinds of things we have.

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.110
Yeah, I get it.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.070
Sharla...

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.560
Are you okay, Sharla?

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:08.590
Yes...

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.030
What was in the shuttle was
the last of the food and water,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.670
one oar, a laser gun (out of energy), and a sewing set.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.990
Luna's backpack, Bell's fanny pack...

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.070
my handkerchief, Sharla's pouch, handkerchief...

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.830
hand soap and candy...

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:27.240
Kaoru had nothing, and Shingo had
a screwdriver set and an exacto knife.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.280
Howard had a hand mirror and comb.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.160
Men like to look good too.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.190
Come to think of it, you had a box.

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:36.770
We can't use that.

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:40.820
So you say, but maybe you're hiding food inside it!

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.040
It's a violin.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.200
A violin?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.080
You brought something like that?

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.480
Let us see!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.380
I refuse! It's important to me.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.330
It has nothing to do with you.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:51.210
Unfair.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.550
Anyways, let's have breakfast.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.670
These are our last rations.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.150
Eat them with that in mind.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:01.350
When we're finished eating, Shingo and Chako
will fix the communications equipment.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.520
Everyone else will split up and look for food and water.

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:06.320
--Okay.
--Got it.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.590
So, I'll go an ahead 'n take a look
at the communication system.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:11.790
You're not going to eat?

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.880
You eat too?

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.160
I run on a fuel cell.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.560
I need Hydrogen.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:22.290
To make Hydrogen, I need to break down the food's sugar.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:25.760
There's too much else in those biscuits,
so they're bad for my body.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.460
So I'll take that thing's share.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.510
You shall not.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:31.840
We'll divide them evenly.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:42.810
Alright, we're done.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.040
My stomach's not full with just this much.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.990
We'll now split up and look for food and water.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.650
I'll look in the forest.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.980
It seems like there might be food there.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.230
Isn't it dangerous in the forest?

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.310
I'll be fine.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:01.630
Carnivorous animals mostly sleep during the day.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:02.930
But...

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:03.770
I'll go too.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:05.980
Kaoru!

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:09.150
Then we'll leave the forest to Bell and Kaoru.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.450
We don't know what you'll find there, so take the knife.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.350
Luna and Sharla will take the cape over there.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.710
Howard and I will go down the beach on this side.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:20.460
I'm going too?

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:21.410
Obviously!

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.750
Luna, look for a river.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.060
If you can find a river, then we'll have a water supply.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:32.780
And whether you find anything or not,
come back before it gets dark.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.370
Obey this first and foremost.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:35.440
Roger!

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:36.170
Got it.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.560
Then we shall depart.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.280
Sharla, let's go.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:47.190
Howard, we're going!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:48.960
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.790
Everyone, be careful!

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:03.730
Bell!

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.580
Just in case.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:29.120
Yeesh! Why do I have to come along?

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.460
Stop grumbling and walk faster!

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.640
I know!

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:36.770
Help me!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:39.320
Huh?

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:46.220
Hey! Don't tell the others about this!

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.460
Now I'm soaking wet.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:36.080
Isn't the sea great? It calms you down just by looking at it.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:39.110
And also the smell...

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.080
What's wrong?

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.580
We're all going to die here anyway.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:47.420
Sharla...

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:21.640
This one's wrecked too... It's worse than I expected.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:23.680
Chako! How's it over there?

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:26.870
Chako?

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:29.910
Chako!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.230
Chako! Chako! Wake up!

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:37.800
Shingo...

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.180
That's a relief. Are you okay?

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.450
Oh, I just felt a little tired.

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:46.990
Short on fuel?

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:50.760
Just stay still. I'll deal with the communications equipment.

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:53.420
Don't be silly!

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:54.980
I'm the smallest one here.

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:57.690
If I don't try hard now, what's going to happen?

00:13:58.480 --> 00:13:59.180
Watch out!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.210
It's impossible after all.

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.870
It's okay, leave this to me. Chako, you rest.

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:09.830
I might have to use your parts later.

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.880
You gotta be kiddin'!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:24.830
What's wrong?

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:28.220
I don't think we'll find any food in this direction.

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.090
How do you know?

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.560
The shape of the leaves.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:33.080
Leaves?

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.680
Up until now they were round, but these ones are pointed.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:41.790
What grows on these trees is hard,
and not much could eat it.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.270
I think there may still be something the way we came.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.710
My dad taught me this a long time ago.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:50.630
Let's go back.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.840
The footing is bad, so be careful.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:06.770
Sharla!

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:10.540
Sharla!

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:14.420
Sharla, are you okay?

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:17.610
Steady yourself.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:19.070
Can you stand?

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:20.590
Let me take a look.

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:25.390
That's good. You don't seem to be hurt.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.990
Oh my! You're all muddy!

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:38.810
What's wrong?

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:42.360
I want to go back!

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:43.930
Back home!

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:45.320
Sharla...

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.860
I want to see my mom and dad.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:50.780
I want to go home!

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:52.820
We can go back.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:54.150
We definitely can.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.180
How do you know that for sure?

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:58.160
We don't even know where this is!

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:01.200
There nothing to eat, and there are monsters.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:03.360
Sharla...

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.490
We won't get home!
We'll be stuck here for the rest of our lives!

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:09.020
And we'll be eaten by those things and we'll all die!

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:09.710
Sharla!

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.590
Sharla, you can't give up!

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:16.880
We can definitely go home. If we lose hope, we're finished.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.880
As long as we believe it, we can go home.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:24.790
It's okay.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.630
I'm with you.

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:28.240
Luna...

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:31.800
Although I may be a little unreliable.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:34.540
Luna!

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.380
We can definitely go home. We can!

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:43.090
What's wrong?

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:46.560
I smell something good.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:50.400
It's true.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.140
I think it's over there.

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:53.640
Should we take a look?

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.190
It's fruit.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:06.770
I wonder if we can eat it.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.190
Anyways, let's bring it back.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:19.520
Sharla!

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:51.620
No! No, no, no!

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:03.860
Luna!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:06.860
Luna!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:08.740
Run away!

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.460
Luna!

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:18.580
Kaoru! Bell!

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:21.130
Move!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.060
Luna...

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:26.630
Sharla.

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:31.370
Luna!

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:33.370
Luna, I'm so glad!

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:34.590
Sharla...

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.710
Thank you, Sharla.

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:00.810
Okay! This should do it.

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:03.900
Please work properly...

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:09.620
No good.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:14.790
I wonder where I went wrong.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:20.640
Oh yeah! Maybe I could use those parts over there.

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:24.340
Hey, wait up!

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.690
Please wait up! Yeesh.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.460
Hey!

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:35.250
How was it? Did you find water?

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.580
No, there wasn't any.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:38.960
I see.

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.010
How about you?

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:42.750
No good?

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:45.080
We're finally here!

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:47.480
I'm spent.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:49.610
I can't move another step.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:51.210
Weakling.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:53.510
Hey!

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:55.610
Hey!

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:03.660
It's food!

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.250
It was terrible!

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:07.250
What happened to you?

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:08.250
It pulled us by our legs.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:11.290
In the end, this is all you found.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:13.840
But a man-eating plant...

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:17.630
I don't know what would have happened
if Kaoru and Bell hadn't come.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:18.940
Bell?

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:21.880
He probably just got his feet tangled together.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:25.860
That's not true! He was very brave, and strong!

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:28.820
Unlike a certain someone.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:33.380
Well, it doesn't matter. How about we eat?

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:41.330
What is this?

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:43.440
Can we really eat this?

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:48.560
It's... it's food!

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:50.310
Yahoo!

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:55.280
Chako...

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:00.490
Chako!

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.980
Yummy!

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:07.390
A-- are you okay?

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:10.590
No problem at all. The sugar content is perfect, too!

00:22:16.930 --> 00:22:18.730
It's delicious! This'll do great!

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.780
It seems to be fine.

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:25.160
In that case, I suppose we'll all have dinner.

00:22:34.070 --> 00:22:35.610
Thank you, Luna.

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:39.280
I'll try my best.

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:41.250
I'll try my best without giving up.

00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:43.130
Sharla...

00:22:44.910 --> 00:22:45.580
Let's eat.

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:05.440
This is a place where we can't be too careful...

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:10.070
...but to keep living we have to find food, water, and fire.

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:13.710
Really? You're finally goin' deep into the forest?

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:18.790
That's right. No matter what's waiting for us, there's
nothing we can do but keep going straight ahead!

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:23.590
To keep hope alive for tomorrow, advance!

00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:28.630
Next time: We're not playing a game.
